<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- Cleave mark, see design/just+bg.svg. That file's tile composition is the canonical one, so
     instead of re-centring the mark here the group maps its whole 100x100 tile onto the 66-unit
     safe zone (scale 0.66, centred in the 108 canvas). Referencing the safe zone rather than the
     72-unit mask bounds costs 8% of the mark's size and buys two things: the whole bounding box
     stays inside the safe circle under every mask, and the margins stop reading tighter than the
     artwork's on launchers that render adaptive icons large (OxygenOS among them).

     translateX then departs from the tile by +2.58: the tile centres the mark by its bounding box,
     and a right-pointing wedge box-centred reads as leaning left. The correction is the anchor of
     the wedge alone (its area centroid pulled 18.2% back towards the box centre, the play_arrow
     ratio) — the wedge is 79.8% of the ink and is what reads as the figure, whereas anchoring on
     the whole shape lets the detached tail, 20.2% of the ink sitting far bottom-left, pull the
     correction to +4.17 and visibly overshoot to the right. Vertically the whole-shape anchor
     asks for -0.28, i.e. the tile's own placement, so that axis is left alone. -->
